      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The Maple Leafs are tearing down the old frame and measuring the next one. <strong>Seven former Leafs are still unsigned after a month of free agency</strong> - a blunt reminder that this roster is being remade, not merely tweaked, and Toronto has already leaned into the draft with six selections, including No. 1 Gavin McKenna and the late-round swing on Russian defenseman Yaroslav Fedoseyev. The club sits 8th in the Atlantic at 78 points, but that's just the paperwork now; the real story is who fits around Auston Matthews and who doesn't. Matthews, as one headline put it, has the most to prove in 2026-27, because the Leafs need their stars to carry more than reputation. <strong>Watch the cap math and the unsigned holdovers - those two lines will tell you what kind of team Toronto is building next</strong>.",
