      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "A four-run first inning can wreck a night - and it wrecked Toronto's. <strong>Shane Bieber got shelled in the opener and the Blue Jays fell 8-6 to Washington</strong>, a loss that left them at 49-59, fifth in the AL East, 14 games back and staring at a season that keeps sliding the wrong way. Kazuma Okamoto's 24th homer at least gave the lineup a pulse, but the bigger headline is Vladimir Guerrero Jr.'s injury scare, which hangs over a club already wobbling after losing 10 of 14. That's not a contender's track. That's a team bleeding ground while trying to find a spine. There was a brief bright spot in Saturday's 3-2 win, but it vanished fast in the next two nights. <strong>They go back to Washington today at 1:05 p.m. ET, and Toronto needs a clean start - and a healthier Guerrero - just to stop the skid.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 29, 2026"
      },
